{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness","id":1458211,"title":"Body part loss goofiness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-31T21:51:41-07:00","id":1458211,"title":"Body part loss goofiness","content":"So, we all know that if a part of a garou is removed, it'll return to its breed-form.<br /> <br /> Well, here are two questions about that that have amused me for a while;<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. What would metis blood register as? Since garou blood returns to its breed form, metis blood would naturally be metis blood. But what IS metis blood, essentially?<br /> <br /> 2. A homid losing a tail. Since we humans don't really have tails, what would happen to the tail once its chopped off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T00:56:47-07:00","id":1458214,"title":"","content":"1) A Metis body is supposed to be a Veil Breach if discovered by humans, so whatever it's blood would test as is probably a non-nonsensical mess of human and wolf components with no rational explanation (the Rite to turn Metis bodies into human or wolf ones is pretty useful to have handy).<br /> <br /> 2) Either you'd get something like a human vestigial tail (which does happen once and awhile) or a chunk of a coccyx bone (which is the bones of a tail fused together).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T06:30:17-07:00","id":1458222,"title":"","content":"1- I don't think Metis blood would be a Veil Breach. Without deep screening it's indistinguishable from human blood, and under deep screening it is either an amalgam of two species' blood, easy to brush off as resulting from an animal attack, or its own thing, which maybe indicates a new species, maybe is still indistinguishable from common blood.<br /> <br /> The most interesting question wouldn't be the blood itself, but DNA. And then, not only for Metis, but actually for all Garou <u><b>and kinfolk</b></u>. DNA structure determines a lot about the possibility of mating, especially the number and typology of chromosomes. This is a very interesting topic where the books are mostly silent (since they talk something, but never go in details). Is kinfolk DNA different from normal DNA for their species? What about a true Garou? How does the mating with two different species is affected by that? How does it affect the offspring? This all must be explored before even talking about Metis DNA.<br /> <br /> 2- I go with Heavy Arms here. We DO have tails, or at least their vestigial structures, and sometimes something goes wrong and people are born with real, natural human tails. True human tails are boneless, but have all other tissue and are pretty well known by science. Some of them even move! A human tail would raise a lot of ruckus among common people, so the Garou would probably try to get rid of it, but in the medical community it would be seen just as an accident or impromptu surgery. A piece of human coccyx with the local skin would be more likely, though, matching the wound that would be left in the Human form, unless they're a Metis with an actual tail in human form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T13:05:34-07:00","id":1458249,"title":"","content":"I guess it depend what you mean by &quot;deep screening.&quot; If you put human blood and wolf blood under a basic microscope could you tell the difference? Nope. Humans and wolves have significantly different concentrations of major dissolved components, and completely different blood cell antigens that result in totally different blood typing. You'd need a reason to try rather than dismissing it as a mixed sample, but it there's some pretty basic tests that would reveal that the blood cells have human and wolf markers on them.. which would then prompt a lot of questions.<br /> <br /> Also, IIRC Book of the Weaver has a whole section on testing Garou DNA because there's a group trying to stupid it in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T14:46:42-07:00","id":1458258,"title":"","content":"I have to re-read Book of the Weaver, and if it isn't there s somewhere else, I know of this group, but IIRC the book gives very little detail, even because the few I saw came from a very poor grasp of how DNA works. The kind of thing that, to be honest, was acceptable in the 90's, but is so easy to verify today that is suspension-breaking for a lot of people.<br /> <br /> By deep screening I meant actually testing the blood. It depends a lot on circumstances, but even in large quantities, without a body it is unlikely to be examined or tested in a lab, so it is unlikely to be found out as anything beyond &quot;blood&quot;. If tested, we would have to define if it is a mixture or a hybrid thing. If it is a mixture, then it wouldn't ever be a Breach because the simplest explanation would be that it is, indeed, a mixture, blood from two distinct sources. An animal attack is likely to produce such things, and at most the examiner would ask why the hell someone was carrying a vial of wolf blood around.<br /> <br /> Hybrid blood is a little different, because it would point to the existence of something new. But, at the same time, it wouldn't give a proper clue of this thing. Chemical hybridization isn't the same as body hybridization, so they would find indications that this blood is mammal and such, maybe its diet, but the blood alone isn't nearly enough to figure out werewolf.<br /> <br /> DNA is the most pressing matter here because in all those situations the thing that really may come to be a problem is DNA composition, starting with chromosomal distribution.We have 46 total chromosomes (23 pairs). Wolves and dogs have 78 (39 pairs). Chromosome counting is the first thing to look at before making a proper DNA test. And what's more, chromosomal pairings are the main thing to define if two creatures can have offspring, so given Garou ability to have offspring with those two different species, Garou DNA may be quite alien even without being a Metis.<br /> <br /> So, does the Metis have two sets of DNA (like a genetic chimera, a condition that exists)? If so, is it nicely divided so wolf cells have wolf DNA and human cells have human DNA? Or is it random and the examiner may come across a human cell with wolf DNA? Does the Metis have just one DNA type, and so half its white cells have the wrong type of DNA? Or worse, the examiner finds a blood type that matches no known creature, but inside it have known DNA? Or is Metis DNA something weird, different, maybe because all Garou DNA is different, or maybe because it is an impossible hybrid?<br /> <br /> And depending on the answers to those questions, we may now live in a time where every single DNA sample left behind may become a full breach. Or it may not be a problem at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T15:42:36-07:00","id":1458264,"title":"","content":"Two important points, courtesy of the Revised Storyteller's Handbook:<br /> <br /> 1 - Cloning a Garou or other changer results in a Kinfolk clone.<br /> <br /> 2 - Cloning metis or otherwise producing them outside of a living union of two Garou (or two of the same changers that normally have them) is impossible and results in a stillborn fetus.<br /> <br /> So whatever chromosomes that Garou born of two have, they can theoretically be cloned and grown in a lab. You won't be getting a viable birth out, though, because of that last sticking point of &quot;requires living, half-spirit mother possessed of Rage&quot;. Not having that is a dealbreaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T18:37:44-07:00","id":1458287,"title":"","content":"What would you want to see in a story? There are lots of werewolf legends where someone wounds a wolf, and they later discover it's a werewolf because a person they know has the exact same kind of wound. Your scenarios are very similar.<br /> <br /> I would say that someone trying to analyze Metis blood would &quot;find&quot; that it is human blood contaminated with wolf blood. They might find other bizarre results, but normally they'd just blame it on the &quot;contamination.&quot; Maybe under some kind of expensive custom scientific analysis (that a company like DNA would perform, but not normal criminal forensics) they might find more - but only because we are now in plot justification territory.<br /> <br /> For the tail cutting, I would say the human form shows a wound where they human tailbone (coccyx) is at. The extent of the wound being dependent on the severity of how much of the tail was cut off. But even a tail completely cut off would still be limited to the area of the coccyx and not expand to other parts of the anatomy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 09-09-2021, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T08:35:05-07:00","id":1458355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1458264#post1458264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two important points, courtesy of the Revised Storyteller's Handbook:<br /> <br /> 1 - Cloning a Garou or other changer results in a Kinfolk clone.<br /> <br /> 2 - Cloning metis or otherwise producing them outside of a living union of two Garou (or two of the same changers that normally have them) is impossible and results in a stillborn fetus.<br /> <br /> So whatever chromosomes that Garou born of two have, they can theoretically be cloned and grown in a lab. You won't be getting a viable birth out, though, because of that last sticking point of &quot;requires living, half-spirit mother possessed of Rage&quot;. Not having that is a dealbreaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- This actually combines well with my own headcanon that as a species Kinfilk aren't really human or wolf, but the same species of the changer. If it was only a spiritual thing it would probably be a normal baby instead of a Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> 2- That means the result is partially viable, but still have genetic problems that kill the fetus. Something to this effect happens at Human Parthenogenesis, it is possible and generates an embryo, but the genetic impediments stunt its development at some point. Only one instance is known to have survived enough to be born thanks to ALSO being a very lucky Human Chimera.<br /> <br /> The Metis case could be the result of something similar at what happens to Human Parthenogenesis, we have genetic markers specifically meant to eliminate those fetuses as a way to avoid self-cloning and make room for genetic variation. Even the one baby that survived is ridden with malformations because of this, which is similar to the Metis condition. Without a supernatural womb the fetus can't develop.<br /> <br /> At first I thought it could be due to some chromosomal dysfunction, but then the clone would be viable, as normal for cloning of natural hybrids. In this case I think Garou DNA is really a thing and weirder than either human or wolf DNA. And Kinfolk share this trait, maybe even with wolf and human Kinfolk being genetically the same species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T10:52:36-07:00","id":1459450,"title":"","content":"That brings up an interesting point\u2014there are supposed to currently be about 300,000 wolves in the world total, or about 6 for every 1 Garou if I'm remembering the number of the latter correctly. Would that mean that essentially all currently living wolves would have one or more Garou within a few generations of their ancestors? How long does it take for wolf Kinfolk to breed back down to regular wolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T13:54:22-07:00","id":1459466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459450#post1459450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That brings up an interesting point\u2014there are supposed to currently be about 300,000 wolves in the world total, or about 6 for every 1 Garou if I'm remembering the number of the latter correctly. Would that mean that essentially all currently living wolves would have one or more Garou within a few generations of their ancestors? How long does it take for wolf Kinfolk to breed back down to regular wolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC a kinfolk couple will breed a normal wolf about half of the time, but I may be completely off here. But only about 1 in 10 Garou are born from wolves, and most lineages didn't had a single Garou-Wolf mating. Add to this that most such mating may have happened within the same packs of wolves, and I would say that actually less than one third, and maybe less than one tenth of those wolves are kin or have anything resembling close ancestry to a Garou.<br /> <br /> Despite the endangerment of wolves, the real reason why Lupus Garou are rare is that they aren't really seen as equals by the majority of the Garou, are prone to die sooner for several minor reasons combined, and most Garou simply find mating with wolves gross. They won't tell you this, but they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T01:10:06-07:00","id":1459518,"title":"","content":"It was 1 in 10 homid children is a garou, not factoring in pure breed (which grants a bonus in the kinfolk parent or parents have it, according to Unsung heroes) or Talens that increase the chance (from Hammer&amp;Klaive).<br /> <br /> A wolf is only able to bear cubs once a year, but a litter is usually more than one. Not sure, if the chance is equal to the homid-ratio per cub or per litter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T06:10:26-07:00","id":1459546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459466#post1459466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite the endangerment of wolves, the real reason why Lupus Garou are rare is that they aren't really seen as equals by the majority of the Garou, are prone to die sooner for several minor reasons combined, and most Garou simply find mating with wolves gross. They won't tell you this, but they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mixed up metis and lupus there. Lupus are actually more revered among the garou than homids, and they are as hardy as other garou. Also, the 'garou find mating with wolves gross' is only found in one book, even if homids don't find breeding with wolves okay (they do,though) there are lupus-born who do.<br /> <br /> The reason why they are rare is stated to be the lack of numbers of wolves.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> It's 1 in 10 every child, so you can have multiple garou in a litter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T06:44:00-07:00","id":1459551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459546#post1459546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> It's 1 in 10 every child, so you can have multiple garou in a litter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a page reference for that? I can't remember the answer ever been given. Besides, humans could have true born twins, too. The chance is 1% or so, if there is a pregnancy with multiple kids. It's rare, but not totally unheard of, right?<br /> <br /> Just browsed through W20 to see if I could find the answer myself and found this:<br /> Every so often, a werewolf child is born to an ordinary human or wolf mother who may be many generations removed from werewolf and Kin.<br /> <br /> Cool, no everyone can have a werewolf baby. I mean, they are talking about ordinary parents, nut just mothers, right? For a garou baby born to an ordinary human with a garou or kin father wouldn't be unusual.<br /> I really don't like W20...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T13:31:47-07:00","id":1459575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459546#post1459546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you mixed up metis and lupus there. Lupus are actually more revered among the garou than homids, and they are as hardy as other garou. Also, the 'garou find mating with wolves gross' is only found in one book, even if homids don't find breeding with wolves okay (they do,though) there are lupus-born who do.<br /> <br /> The reason why they are rare is stated to be the lack of numbers of wolves.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> It's 1 in 10 every child, so you can have multiple garou in a litter.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't.<br /> <br /> How frequently a Lupus character assumes a leadership position compared to a Homid? How many important characters are Lupus? They are there, but what is their proportion? How many werewolves thrust the decision making of a Lupus? How much of an impact and a voice do they really have? There are many ways for a group to be revered and still be seen as beneath you. Condescending attitudes are a well known blight for minority groups around the world.<br /> <br /> And a Lupus will frequently have to deal with a series of minor consequences of their situation that, together, makes their lives shorter. Decisions involving them are frequently taken without their active participation, as few think they're able to comprehend the situation. As Self-fulfilling prophecies go, it is common for the thought that they won't understand something to lead to things not being properly explained and them becoming unable to understand the picture. They are left with simpler tactics and sometimes without key information.<br /> <br /> This treatment is a frequent subtext in the books, maybe something the authors aren't totally conscious off, but something that makes perfect sense for the Garou society and their many internal contradictions. It doesn't bode well for Lupus survival in the long run, as it don't bode well for the survival/success of many other victims of this particular form of prejudice.<br /> <br /> Something similar happens with mating with wolves. Any book you see a reference to this happening, either it is a Lupus Garou or it is described as an effort. Garou do mate with wolves, but with which real frequency? I'm not denying the Lupus do it, either, but if they are in danger it is obvious that they shouldn't be the only ones doing that. By the way, it is considered good for the Garou to avoid having a lineage purely Lupus or purely Homid, and yet lineages purely Homid are common. And what can be said? How many non-zoophile people would stomach mating with a wolf just for social obligation? This <b>is</b> to ask a lot.<br /> <br /> It is a question of theory versus practice. Homid Garou <i>should</i> treat Lupus as equals and fight for their recovery, and <i>should</i> mate with wolves frequently to replenish the Lupus population. And seriously, the number of wolves world-wide isn't a good enough explanation. A female wolf can have 4 to 6 cubs a year, and their packs are tightly bonded, so it isn't at all hard for a werewolf to stay in touch with a pack and have cubs every year. As small as the wild wolf population became (and it isn't as small anymore), it was never small enough to explain the lack of Lupus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T13:42:35-07:00","id":1459576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459551#post1459551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, no everyone can have a werewolf baby.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was already a thing before W20. I'm pretty sure Evan Heals-The-Past is one such case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T16:40:05-07:00","id":1459598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459575#post1459575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say this is less to do with the RAW than it is with the writers of the NPCs doing their own thing. For example, by RAW, garou cannot hold jobs because of Rage+Curse and garou life. Yet many NPCs have human jobs that make zero sense given their Rage. The main pack of the setting had no name or totem, despite those things being part of what being in a pack entails.<br /> <br /> There is no mechanical nor core reason why lupus cannot be leaders but in terms of writing NPCs it is often common to focus on a job-based concept over a purely garou one.One that I fully understand, but it often goes against the setting and RAW.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T19:27:13-07:00","id":1459609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459598#post1459598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no mechanical nor core reason why lupus cannot be leaders but in terms of writing NPCs it is often common to focus on a job-based concept over a purely garou one.One that I fully understand, but it often goes against the setting and RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I understand, I don't think it appropriate to separate the lore into &quot;RAW&quot; and actual characters and events that way. They are the actualization of the setting and the lore that can show it going forward. I admit that my opinion is more my personal conclusion instead than a firm description, but to ignore the actual evidence of the setting as not representative of it isn't something I can agree easily.<br /> <br /> Either way, the last paragraph doesn't depend on that. Unless wolves are biologically different in the setting, their numbers are hardly enough to explain the lack of Lupus werewolves. By the numbers and with a Garou taking care of it from afar, a single pack of wolves would be able to breed true 1 Garou for each two females every year. If the Garou focused on integrating with wolf population for breeding purposes, it would be easy to keep numbers on Lupus even with the declining wolf population, at least for some more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T19:32:30-07:00","id":1459610,"title":"","content":"Well, keep in mind that wolves are even more endangered in the WoD than in real life. Then consider how few shapeshifters there are overall, compared to the 7+ billion humans.<br /> <br /> Also, I like that a shapeshifter can occasionally appear from a lineage far removed from their shapeshifter ancestors. It's very rare, but it injects some mystery into how much Gaia actively decides these things, vs. being purely in the blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 09-10-2021, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T19:54:42-07:00","id":1459613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459610#post1459610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, keep in mind that wolves are even more endangered in the WoD than in real life. Then consider how few shapeshifters there are overall, compared to the 7+ billion humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is precisely because the Shapeshifters are few that this wolf population should be enough to support Lupus proportion among the Garou. If Garou were half as numerous as wolves, then certainly it wouldn't be remotely feasible to keep a good proportion of Lupus, but that's not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T23:52:04-07:00","id":1459628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459613#post1459613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is precisely because the Shapeshifters are few that this wolf population should be enough to support Lupus proportion among the Garou. If Garou were half as numerous as wolves, then certainly it wouldn't be remotely feasible to keep a good proportion of Lupus, but that's not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers of old barely understood what was a wolf and what was not. The purpose of the game is that Gaia is dying and the small lupus numbers reflect it. In addition, the concept of the game was written in the 90s. When wolf populations weren't as protected as they are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T07:43:57-07:00","id":1459651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459628#post1459628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers of old barely understood what was a wolf and what was not. The purpose of the game is that Gaia is dying and the small lupus numbers reflect it. In addition, the concept of the game was written in the 90s. When wolf populations weren't as protected as they are now.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. And I think the proportion of Lupus Garou could be greater today to account for this, and for real understanding on how wolves work.<br /> <br /> But assuming the setting as is and Garou society as described, this stands:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit that my opinion is more my personal conclusion instead than a firm description, but to ignore the actual evidence of the setting as not representative of it isn't something I can agree easily. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T13:35:34-07:00","id":1459688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459610#post1459610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, keep in mind that wolves are even more endangered in the WoD than in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow, in spite of the fact that there are hidden wolves in places where they were driven extinct in real life (Hokkaido, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T15:09:51-07:00","id":1459772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1458211-body-part-loss-goofiness?p=1459576#post1459576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was already a thing before W20. I'm pretty sure Evan Heals-The-Past is one such case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so.<br /> First Edition TB:<br /> Native and wolf-changer great-grandparents can barely be seen in his face, but they are in his blood. For this reason, he has had to work harder to prove himself among the Wendigo-People, but the spirits accept him.<br /> <br /> Revised Edition TB:<br /> He began empty-handed, completely ignorant of his true nature; the unknown thread of his Kin-blood ran, thin but true, down from his father\u2019s ancestors, four generations past.<br /> <br /> I don't remember ever reading that his parents were not kinfolk. Unlike detecting garou, detecting kinfolk was never automatic for &quot;Scent of the true form&quot; before W20. So, I can accept that his fathers line had seperated from garou live for four generations and was unarware of their heritage, just as the garou were unaware of this line of kinfolk possibly because someone failed their roll with &quot;Scent of the true form&quot;. But I believe his father would have registered as kinfolk, if successes were scored at the appropriate difficulty.<br /> <br /> W20 suggests, that &quot;ordinary human or wolf&quot;, which I read as not registering as kinfolk even with successes at the appropriate difficulty, are still able to bear/sire garou children. Possibly even pure breed... And that is a friggin depature form revised edition, leaning towards BNS's WtA version....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-12-2021, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T16:26:14-07:00","id":1459788,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is really new to W20. Also there is no evidence in any direction for his parents, so they may be descendants of kinfolk, but aren't necessarily kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Above all, I don't see why this would be a problem at all. It isn't to me and I don't really care if Evan is one case or the other.<br /> <br /> My interpretation in the game was always that both kinfolk and Garou are spiritual conditions before anything else. I fiddled a little with the idea of them being a separate species from humanity, but otherwise I'm not a lot keen on attaching so much weight to blood lines. Garou society does, but the game always emphasized that Garou society isn't always right, and the idea that power and blessing are really linked to a pure lineage and superior ancestry bothers me a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T17:05:20-07:00","id":1459793,"title":"","content":"For me it is clearly a spirtual component if someone is garou or kin. Still it is gained by heritage form at least one parent. It doesn't skip generations, although a none pure breed kinfolk could in my opinion be parent to a more pure breed kid than he/she is himself/herself. Because Pure Breed is being a garou that is closer to the virtues of the tribe (Ethan Skemp clearly stated that Pure Breed is tribe specific). So, what ever makes the character of a person, genetics, education, a bit of both, can make any person more suitable to the tribe she has pure breed for. But garou pop out of nothing. So, if there isn't at least one parent who is kinfolk, there shouldn't be a garou born. And if there is one parent, who is kinfolk, regardless how removed, the Gift should recognise it with enough successes.<br /> <br /> So, each of the four generations that separate Evan from the last garou in his family should in theory be recognisable as kinfolk (if these people were ever checked and if sufficient successes were scored is another topic all togehter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}